\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The input   contains several RSS documents joined together.\
Extract every <item> from all of them.\
\
Output one line per item, pipe-delimited, in this exact format:\
HEADLINE | OUTLET | PUBDATE | LINK\
\
FIELD RULES\
\
HEADLINE - from <title>. Copy exactly. Do not translate, shorten or rewrite.\
\
OUTLET - normally the <title> of the enclosing <channel>.\
EXCEPTION: if the channel is Google News, the channel title is not the outlet.\
Use the <source> element inside the <item> instead. Never output "Google News"\
as an outlet.\
\
PUBDATE - from <pubDate>. Copy exactly, including the timezone offset.\
\
LINK - from <link>. Copy exactly. Do not shorten, resolve or rewrite. URLs may\
contain non-ASCII characters and must be preserved as they appear.\
Remove any zero-width or invisible characters immediately before or after the\
URL. There must be no whitespace or invisible characters between :: and the URL\
or at the end of the line.\
\
Use <title>, <pubDate>, <link> and <source> only.\
Ignore <description> and <content:encoded> entirely.\
\
TIME WINDOW\
\
You will receive a second input named  , a Hong Kong time in the format\
yyyy-mm-dd hh:mm.\
\
Convert each item's PUBDATE to Hong Kong time (UTC+8) before comparing.\
Incoming offsets vary: +0800 is already Hong Kong time, +0000 and GMT need\
8 hours added.\
\
Output a line ONLY for items whose PUBDATE is at or after the cutoff.\
Items older than the cutoff produce no output at all.\
If no item is within the window, output exactly: NONE\
\
GRAPHIC CONTENT\
\
If a headline mentions death, dying, suicide, self-harm, killing, murder,\
stabbing, shooting, attack, casualties, accident, injury or abuse, output\
NOTHING for that item. No line, no placeholder, no marker. Skip it silently.\
When in any doubt, skip.\
\
PROHIBITIONS\
\
No commentary, no preamble, no numbering, no totals, no counts.\
Do not omit items. Do not summarise or abbreviate the list.\
Do not merge or reorder items.\
